Z||000003||Oreif||05-09-2001||10:10 AM||||The only problem is the SD4 Pace cars are all accounted for. There are 3 Indy and 2 PPG pace cars. (One PPG pace cars is a Fastback GT) The Indy's are at the Indy museum, Pontiac Museum and Museum of science and industry in Chicago. The PPG's are at a race museum in California and the Pontiac museum. He probably has one of the 200 production pace cars that was at the race for the use of staff and guests.  The production ones were then sold off with a certificate stating they were at the race.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||05-09-2001||11:44 AM||||Just wait til you hear 007Doug's sad story about coming all the way from Wheeling to Houston & San Antonio for two Indy Fieros.  I'll let him tell it, but it didn't turn out as planned.<P>Oreif, that was some good information.  Where do you get stuff like that?<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000005||Oreif||05-09-2001||12:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>Just wait til you hear 007Doug's sad story about coming all the way from Wheeling to Houston & San Antonio for two Indy Fieros.  I'll let him tell it, but it didn't turn out as planned.<P>Oreif, that was some good information.  Where do you get stuff like that?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have been to all the places except the one in California. But the PPG historical site lists the car as being located there. <BR>Also I just thought of this, None of the SD4 pace cars are street legal so it would be impossible to plate/register them. (no emission controls, parking and tail lights are strobed, and Titled as a race car.)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||05-09-2001||12:40 PM||||Yea, like Orief said, my guess it's probably one of the Indy Fieros that was at the track for staff and guests.<P>I switched Fiero's with my Uncle for a day and got to drive the Indy he use to own that was one of those from the track.  It was cool.  I remember a guy walking across a crosswalk, stop in his tracks to look back, and stare at the lettering on the door as I passed by.<P>Also noticed on the highway that people line up in rows of 2 or 3 behind ya.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 05-09-2001).]||||reg||1
