Z||000032||Oreif||05-14-2001||09:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>they are low 2500 and less so i guess i am not alone.<BR>btw when i checked Kruse site for indy prices<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's funny, The Fiero Price guide, Hemmings, and Volo price guides, All show the Indy Fiero in average to excellent as being priced out at $4000 to $6500. These are from sites that know what a collectable car is worth. The Indy pace car replica's (all types) were not advertised as being the "fastest" of a particular car, Just a limited production run of the cars. <P>BTW ~ I just went thru the Kruse website. They Auctioned off an Indy Fiero with 33,000 miles on it for $11,822.00 (Final Bid Price)<BR>I could not find a "price guide" on-line. You had to buy a book. Also this is the same group that sold an 84 SE with 178 miles on it thru Ebay last year and got $14,500 for it. <P>So it looks like your alone....again.<P>||||reg||1
