Z||000035||Oreif||05-15-2001||08:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>when did that indy sell i checked prices of fiero's around the first of the year and only saw 2 indys sold in 2000 at kruse one was 2500 the other less. may have missed one.<BR>but i will bet if the alcoa car comes up for sale it will get more than any other fiero ever inc the real pace cars. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So what, This is a "FIERO" forum not an Alcoa forum. A 1969 Pontiac Trans Am Convertable was auctioned off last year for $125,000 (Only 8 were made and only 5 are still confirmed to be around) There are plenty of other cars that will draw even more money at an auction, But we are only concerned about Fiero's. This thread is about the "Holy Grail of Fiero's" Not the Holy Grail of all automobiles. Sheesh, will you at least try to stay on topic just once.<P>||||reg||1
