Z||000063||Steve Normington||05-17-2001||01:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2xsess:<BR>"Witthhh a Herring" damn, I can't remember that whole line.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>TMBK, the line is... "You must chop down the tallest oak with... a Herring."<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2xsess:<BR>It was the knights who say niegh.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"No, no, you're not doing it right. It's nee! No, no, from the lips. Nee! Nee!"<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR>Father:<BR>Listen, lad. I built some of these Fieros back up from nothing. When I started here, all there was was busted panels, cracked windshields, blown heads, torn aero bumpers and such. Other kings said I was daft to build a wankel engine into a Fiero, but I built it all the same, just to show 'em. It snapped in two in just a few hours. So, I built a second one. That snapped in two. So, I built a third one. That burned up, flipped over, then snapped in two, but the fourth one... stayed running! And that's what you're gonna get, lad. The only running wankel powered Fiero in these islands.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OMG, ROTFLMFAO. That is the funniest thing I've seen in a long time. May I use that?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000064||Slammed Fiero||05-17-2001||01:58 AM||||I hadn't been paying attention to this thread , but just decided to take a look now<P>I see some of you have gotten onto the topic of Alcan Aluminum space frame Fiero. <P>A long time family friend is pretty high up at Alcan , He is the reason I got to drive a 2 million dollar mercury sable. The car was all aluminum with a SHO motor and a 5spd , some 700lbs lighter than stock. I asked him about the Aluminum Fiero's he says he has seen one in person and has pics of it. Last he heard it was located in a warehouse. He say the car 2 years ago according to the date on the Pics he says. <P>As soon as I get them I will be sure to post. The car is a Siver GT FB with a Quad 4 as mentioned earlier. He said the car only has a few miles , and unfortunatley isn't likely to ever go anywhere out of Alcans warehouse or possession. He saw it while they were doing inventory and he had to document his own projects.<P><BR> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
